{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator continuity constraint: every change must preserve workflows/environments that depend on old vocabulary. Additive foundations keep legacy commands fully functional; any rename/removal must migrate all in-repo workflow, environment, script, config, test, and documentation consumers in the same shippable change. Operator also authorizes Gerrit relation stacks submitted together once multiple tickets are complete. Epic plan updated: final verb set explicitly includes check-access, four operational flags are named, and continuity/stacking is a standing decision."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786142571498301001,"uuid":"cd2ee204-92dd-4c25-9ce6-4f75a2f01a06"}